  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, with Marcus Cole as the project leader. The project kicked off in Q3 2023, with an initial meeting on July 15th. Key developments include a budget approval of $2M by the executive board, though a later update noted an adjustment to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses to cover real-time analytics integration. The project involves leveraging AI for data visualization and exploring partnerships with TechInnovate. Milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Feedback has been requested from stakeholders regarding prototypes and strategies, with deadlines ranging from July to November. Security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. Additionally, a team named 'Zenith Innovations' was onboarded for a 'Revolutionary AI Project' with an onboarding session on April 15th, 2023."
